    "body": "Escalated from effort:high to effort:max. Claim released.\n\nThe requested continuous workflow is unsupported on upstream/main 8719d8b7.\nThe pin `microarc4_continuous_walkthrough_posts_without_refusal` failed on unchanged production code.\nCommand: `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test microarc4_walkthroughs`.\nIt sends A0 and A10 in one section through the shipped machine file and `tormach.cps`.\nThe post reports: \"simultaneous 4-axis motion (A changes inside the operation) - not confirmed on PathPilot; this post indexes A between operations only\".\n\n`assets/posts/tormach.cps:626-628` contains this intentional refusal.\nCommit f99f045e introduced the indexing support and this restriction.\nThe source identifies PathPilot rollover and combined-feed handling as unconfirmed.\nThe continuous guide also lists drawing wrapping and inverse-time feed as unimplemented.\nThe microARC machine file declares no A feed cap.\n\nThe indexed demo already exists in `docs/tester-kits/tormach-microarc-4th/`.\nThe complete request still needs wrapping behavior and confirmed continuous posting before simulator validation.\nNew algorithm work and unresolved controller behavior match effort:max.\nRemoving the refusal would not establish correct output.\n\nNo production code changed. No PR was opened. No PathPilot Hub run was performed.\nThe quick gate, clippy, and mutation checks were not run because no fix was made.\nNo goldens changed. The planned files have no open PR overlap.\nThe local reproduction is saved at `/tmp/1904-microarc4-walkthroughs.rs`.\nCopy it to `crates/post/tests/microarc4_walkthroughs.rs` to repeat the command.\nThe failure output is saved at `/tmp/1904-pin-red.log`.\nThese local files are not committed.\n",
